 people into space over  the past couple of years  mark zuckerberg calls it living in the  future the metaverse aims to be a  virtual universe where users from around  the world can interact in immersive  digital spaces it's still being  developed and is a little rough around  the edges but that hasn't stopped tech  giants brands and even everyday people  from rushing to build and invest kayla  mclean has been working on this story  for the new reality  kayla in what's being described as the  next evolution of the internet the race  is on to develop the virtual world of  the future some investing thousands and  even millions into real estate and one  of them is a diner owner from montreal  david minikucci has only been the owner  of the famous cosmos for less than two  years but he's been going to the  montreal diner since he was a teenager  he decided to buy the restaurant because  it holds a lot of sentimental value for  him david wanted to expand the brand but  not with another bricks and mortar  location  instead david spent close to fifteen  thousand dollars to buy land in the  metaverse and open a virtual cosmos you  know i'm an entrepreneur i i want to you  know grow the business just like anybody  else would want to do but at the same  time i truly have an emotional  attachment to this place and i'll never  change what we actually do here  david is just one of many people whether  investors or tech giants racing to own a  piece of virtual land and investing in  the future of the metaverse it's  expected to be a multi-trillion dollar  revenue opportunity  there are a handful of online platforms  that offer metaverse experiences  some owned by companies and others that  are community driven for example  decentraland sandbox and horizon worlds  rn mani also known as mr who's the boss  is a youtube tech expert based in the uk  so i like to define it as it's not an  internet that you're looking at through  a screen it's an internet that you're  inside of one of t